From 4fa8ab6d59e3003a8e4b1b7fd15f6373a8656575 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:11:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Write Remix options through the Remix API behind the
 developer gate

RTXFixesBinary's RemixConfig.SetConfigVariable takes only the options the
RTX package's own Lua sets (the native loader's ADR 0234): any server's
client scripts and any add-on reach it. Remix.SetConfig and SetDebugView
wrote through that function whatever gate the call had passed, so debug
views and the replacement switches were refused to developers too.

Behind the developer mutation gate (local single-player decided natively,
sv_cheats 1, -insecure) the module now writes rtx.* options through the
Remix API itself: d3d9.dll's remixapi_InitializeLibrary, asked once at the
first such write, initialized with the headers RTXFixesBinary and RTX
Water use (0.1000.1), never Startup or Shutdown. Without that gate the
client rendering gate still forwards to RemixConfig, whose list decides;
names that are not rtx.* options are refused on both routes
(Policy::RouteConfig). A restore goes back the way its value went in,
even after the gate has closed (Policy::RestoreThroughApi), and at the
module's close a value written through the API is restored through it
even when RTXFixesBinary is gone. Overrides and SessionConfig name each
override's route. Version 0.2.2 (the native loader's ADR 0237).

render_policy_test.cpp checks the route composed with the session gate:
a copy of the policy that sends every write to RemixConfig (the module
before this change) fails it, and so does one that sends every write to
the API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
